 kinase binding activity. Involved in several processes, including G1/S transition of mitotic cell cycle; positive regulation of cell population proliferation; and positive regulation of protein kinase activity. Located in nucleoplasm. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q5MJ70","text":"Regulates the G1/S phase transition of the cell cycle by binding and activating CDK1 and CDK2 (PubMed:12972555). Contributes to CDK2 activation without promoting CDK2 phosphorylation, by inducing a conformation change of the CDK2 T-loop that obstructs the substrate-binding cleft prior to kinase activation (PubMed:28666995). Mediates cell survival during the DNA damage process through activation of CDK2 (PubMed:12839962)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}